"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/667874-seems-there-are-more-seemings?p=667944#post667944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder what the chaos seeming might be called. Tying to think of appropriate names, but not having much luck.<br /> <br /> Jesters, Fools?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fools works for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:21:47-07:00","id":668741,"title":"","content":"Both of those are good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T14:57:53-07:00","id":668851,"title":"","content":"Thing is though, it doesn't really sound fae-like to me. Beast, Fairest, Wizened, Darkling and Ogre all sound like something you'd expect from the fairy lands. Another idea I was thinking of was Rumpelstiltskin, but that seemed a bit too long compared to the other names. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T16:24:45-07:00","id":668957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/667874-seems-there-are-more-seemings#post667874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to hear what you guys think, especially if you have more dirt from other postings!</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I've always found it useful to get more stuff in one place. I think <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/611222-the-hedge-supplement-book\">the thread</a> on the Hedge Supplement book was the first place Dave talked about Seemings 7 and 8 in any real detail. I think I got the main beats from that conversation in the spoiler box below. Dave encapsulated the heart of them in the blog you quoted, but you'll indeed find some more flesh to put on them.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/611222-the-hedge-supplement-book?p=622002#post622002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spoiler alert.<br /> <br /> I'm not 100% sure the eighth will go in Hedge yet. Not sure. Probably. But, thinking.<br /> <br /> The seventh, for Grimm's Fairy Tales Lost, is someone that leveraged the power of stories to escape. They played a part. They internalised a tale, because tales are a language the Gentry have to listen to.<br /> <br /> The eighth, if I end up doing it, is someone that wilfully and fully abandoned herself to luck. Not someone that escaped by pure chance. But someone that literally relied on random chance, who saw a choice, and chose chaos. This is someone that saw an open, dark well, and thought, &quot;There's a chance I could survive,&quot; then shrugged and jumped.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/611222-the-hedge-supplement-book?p=622422#post622422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of thought that was what all the Seemings were doing - they were divided based on the specific story.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/611222-the-hedge-supplement-book?p=622846#post622846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's KIND of the opposite. You're in their story, and you just say, &quot;Enough. This is where I take authorial control. MASSIVE REWRITE, FUCKER.&quot;<br /> <br /> Whereas this Seeming plays along to win. She looks for the right, narratively appropriate story beats to win. It's the difference between taking control by forcing the story to change, and taking control by actively deciding to play along.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/611222-the-hedge-supplement-book?p=623822#post623822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) They're absolutely 2e. The old Seeming model would be almost impossible to support with additional Seemings, because you would have to devote so much space to adding Kiths in order to make them even comparable to the existing ones.<br /> <br /> 2) We're calling them Grimms', after the famous brothers. This Seeming didn't necessarily begin in the early part of the nineteenth century, and it most certainly didn't end there. But it became something worth noticing there; the people knew the language of the Gentry in a whole new way. I don't have a name for the eighth Seeming yet.<br /> <br /> 3) Seventh Seeming is my Changeling: The Lost Akira Kurosawa homage.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/611222-the-hedge-supplement-book?p=639132#post639132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm considering [Loyalists] a Seeming. They did escape, but their choice was to abandon one kind of captivity for another.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/611222-the-hedge-supplement-book?p=639472#post639472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Loyalists are a Seeming, then wouldn't that make Grimms the 8th, and the Risktaking Seeming the 9th Seeiming?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/611222-the-hedge-supplement-book?p=639611#post639611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically yes.<br /> <br /> But I don't count [Loyalists] amongst the list when I talk about the other two, because the assumption is, they're not by default intended for players. That's not to say you couldn't play one or whatever. Just that the game assumes you're playing someone who broke free.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/611222-the-hedge-supplement-book?p=639826#post639826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loyalist Seeming comes from making the choice to serve as method of escape. If you don't make that choice, you're Seemingless.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T19:13:40-07:00","id":669133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/667874-seems-there-are-more-seemings?p=668104#post668104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, will the Grimms have rules for the 2nd edition only? It seems strange since the &quot;Lily, Sabre and Thorn&quot; chapter of the main book will use the rules of the 1rst edition only.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because it was written over a year ago, and this material was written last month. <br /> <br /> I can't put 1e rules in there for it, because space reasons, also because Seemings mean something completely different, and because Seemings take way more words to cover in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T23:30:47-07:00","id":669299,"title":"","content":"Just for curiositys sake, is there anywhere where you can neatly read a list of all the announced seemings with a few sentances long description of who they are and why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T00:31:55-07:00","id":669311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/667874-seems-there-are-more-seemings?p=667917#post667917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that what they're called? That's a fairly loaded word, so it's surprising to me that they used it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/667874-seems-there-are-more-seemings?p=667940#post667940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's in the name of the Era.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i><b>Grimms</b></i> maybe a good name for the Era and from it, up to modern times. <b>B</b><b>ut how this Seeming would be called before?</b> Because I think that &quot;changelings that internalized tales&quot; would be in history from the dawn of times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T07:56:23-07:00","id":669672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/667874-seems-there-are-more-seemings?p=669311#post669311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Grimms</b></i> maybe a good name for the Era and from it, up to modern times. <b>B</b><b>ut how this Seeming would be called before?</b> Because I think that &quot;changelings that internalized tales&quot; would be in history from the dawn of times.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Dave, they have been, but they were considerably rarer before the Era. The publication of Grimm's Fairy Tales brought the structure of the Fae's stories into the public consciousness, so abductees were more familiar with the laws of Arcadia and better equipped to turn the role their keeper gave them to their advantage. I wouldn't be surprised if they never had a name before that, just because they were such oddities prior to Grimm's stories. I wouldn't even be surprised if they were often mistaken for Loyalists.<br /> <br /> &quot;What do you mean you played along with your Keeper's story? How could you even have escaped without subverting it?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-18-2015, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:16:10-07:00","id":670072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/667874-seems-there-are-more-seemings?p=669672#post669672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to Dave, they have been, but they were considerably rarer before the Era. The publication of Grimm's Fairy Tales brought the structure of the Fae's stories into the public consciousness, so abductees were more familiar with the laws of Arcadia and better equipped to turn the role their keeper gave them to their advantage. I wouldn't be surprised if they never had a name before that, just because they were such oddities prior to Grimm's stories. I wouldn't even be surprised if they were often mistaken for Loyalists.<br /> <br /> &quot;What do you mean you played along with your Keeper's story? How could you even have escaped without subverting it?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What about in campaigns not set in western countries, where the stories are told all the time or recorded elsewhere? Presumably Changelings based on Taoist fables who lived through a story recorded in the Liezi would be around prior to the Brothers Grimm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:31:52-07:00","id":670096,"title":"","content":"Dunno. We'll have to see what Dark Eras says on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:43:51-07:00","id":670123,"title":"","content":"For the Loyalist seeming, how will they looks? I mean, one of the perk of the first edition Loyalist is that they can be anyone, since it's separate from the Seeming. Now that they are a Seeming like the Darkling or the Fairest, how will they pass as anything else since it will be written on their face that they are the willing slaves of the Gentry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T14:30:52-07:00","id":670176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/667874-seems-there-are-more-seemings?p=670123#post670123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Loyalist seeming, how will they looks? I mean, one of the perk of the first edition Loyalist is that they can be anyone, since it's separate from the Seeming. Now that they are a Seeming like the Darkling or the Fairest, how will they pass as anything else since it will be written on their face that they are the willing slaves of the Gentry?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave mentioned that it's not always obvious at a glance what Seeming a particular Changeling has. Given a pretty tiger person made of fire, is that Changeling an Elemental, a Beast, a Fairest, or Seemingless? One or more of those traits could be owed to several Seemings, Kiths, lingering elements from the Changeling's Durance, or (to a lesser extent) other properties (e.g. Striking Looks).<br /> <br /> My guess is Loyalist identifying features wouldn't be too obvious. They might look either no different from or hard to tell apart from someone without a Seeming. Hmm... A Changeling's Keeper typically already made him the way it wanted him, so I could see a case for a Loyalist either looking just the same or assuming a more extreme take on his Kith. Where &quot;more extreme&quot; is tricky to judge, unless one had seen the Changeling before he became a Loyalist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T17:41:37-07:00","id":670344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/667874-seems-there-are-more-seemings?p=669672#post669672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to Dave, they have been, but they were considerably rarer before the Era. The publication of Grimm's Fairy Tales brought the structure of the Fae's stories into the public consciousness, so abductees were more familiar with the laws of Arcadia and better equipped to turn the role their keeper gave them to their advantage. I wouldn't be surprised if they never had a name before that, just because they were such oddities prior to Grimm's stories. I wouldn't even be surprised if they were often mistaken for Loyalists.<br /> <br /> &quot;What do you mean you played along with your Keeper's story? How could you even have escaped without subverting it?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, but didn't the Grimm version of those stories end horrendously for the main character? It wasn't until Mother Goose came along that they were turned into kid friendly tales and nursery rhymes. In fact, practically all fairy tales had horrendous endings or terrifying plots. That's kind of why they were used to keep children in line.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think Goldilockes gets eaten by the bears, Red Riding Hood and her grandmother are both killed by the wolf. Hansel and Grettle were abandoned by their parents not because their mother was evil, but because it was a time of famine and they could no longer feed the entire family. I've heard two different versions, one saying they were killed by the witch and the other saying they escaped, only to find out their parents were dead. The Little Mermaid turns into foam, Quasimodo is stoned to death while Esmerelda is hung. I think Aladin is also killed because it's Arabia and he's a thief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-18-2015, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T18:25:03-07:00","id":670365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/667874-seems-there-are-more-seemings?p=670344#post670344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, but didn't the Grimm version of those stories end horrendously for the main character?</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to have a highly idealized understanding of the Fae worldview re: protagonism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T18:53:13-07:00","id":670402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/667874-seems-there-are-more-seemings?p=670344#post670344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong, but didn't the Grimm version of those stories end horrendously for the main character? It wasn't until Mother Goose came along that they were turned into kid friendly tales and nursery rhymes. In fact, practically all fairy tales had horrendous endings or terrifying plots. That's kind of why they were used to keep children in line.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think Goldilockes gets eaten by the bears, Red Riding Hood and her grandmother are both killed by the wolf. Hansel and Grettle were abandoned by their parents not because their mother was evil, but because it was a time of famine and they could no longer feed the entire family. I've heard two different versions, one saying they were killed by the witch and the other saying they escaped, only to find out their parents were dead. The Little Mermaid turns into foam, Quasimodo is stoned to death while Esmerelda is hung. I think Aladin is also killed because it's Arabia and he's a thief.</div> </div> </div> </div>Little Red Riding Hood and Hansel and Gretel are the only Grimm fairy tales in that list, and Mother Goose was a collection of nursery rhymes, not fairy tales. And while older versions of most popular fairy tales were much darker, they didn't all end badly for the protagonist. In fact, more often it was the villain that met with a greusome end.<br /> <br /> At any rate, a changeling is most likely <i>not</i> the protagonist of the story their Keeper writes them into. If they were, they wouldn't need to re-write the story to make it their own and reclaim agency. It sounds like Grimms, conversely, will play along with their Keeper's story, but use its narrative conventions to subvert or twist the story to suit their own needs. The popularity of Grimm's Fairy Tales merely helped to spread the general knowledge of those storytelling conventions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-18-2015, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T05:24:52-07:00","id":671826,"title":"","content":"Was literacy common amongst those cultures? Because the publications by Grim (and their colleagues in other countries who published their works around the same time) did coexist with a marked increase in literacy in Europe. Simply writing down a story does not mean a wider audience actually gets to know it... (My knowledge on Indian, Chinese and Japanese history beyond the broad strokes is not very good though.)<br /> <br /> As for Grimm, they themselves actually changed their own stories to adopt them to a wider crowd, although they mostly removed the sexual content (the original versions of the fairy tells are quite lewd with babies sucking needles out their mother's hands to wake them up from that century long sleep instead of a prince's kiss) they also worked on the endings. Those stories that served as lessons btw still had happy endings, especially for those following the rules. Their intent after all was partially to teach people that it is good to follow the rules <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Finally, I did not pay much attention to the Dark Ages, but considering their first story was published in 1812, several centuries after what we in general call the Dark Ages, I am a bit curious. Mind you, Napoleon and the Industrial Revolution are great settings for a campaign, but I just read Dark Ages and dismissed it as an interesting product for me. The Dark Ages as a setting do not have a big draw on me. So why call the product Dark Ages? Then again, I am probably missing something...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","user":"Madfox11","date":". 09-20-2015, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T05:34:33-07:00","id":671828,"title":"","content":"It's an evocative title because of how long the term has been around, but it's also a play on words. World of Darkness, Ages from the World of Darkness, Dark Ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T05:44:02-07:00","id":671833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/667874-seems-there-are-more-seemings?p=671828#post671828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an evocative title because of how long the term has been around, but it's also a play on words. World of Darkness, Ages from the World of Darkness, Dark Ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I have too much of an interest in real history for theses associations, mine just sticks at 500 to 1400 when I read the Dark Ages* <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> O well, I might want to take a look at the product in that case once it becomes available <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> * And I am well aware historians don't tend to use the term now-a-days anyway <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T05:45:56-07:00","id":671834,"title":"","content":"The title's actually Dark Eras, covering a variety of time periods. Dark Ages is the CWoD, covering the first half of the 13th century CE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T05:52:41-07:00","id":671842,"title":"","content":"I think the only era that is actually set during the dark ages, is the black death era from the companion. But even that is only the case when taking a broad definition of dark ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T12:30:36-07:00","id":672290,"title":"","content":"The Grimm Seeming sounds perfect for my laser disc game escapee. At the end of her last game, she got into her van and drove off, just as Lance does. Then she keeps driving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","c